gradle-wrapper.jar
/.gradle
/captures/
/gradlew
/gradlew.bat
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# ...with one deliberate exception. `dev-keystore.jks` is a throwaway key that
# exists so every CI build is signed identically and a new dev build installs
# over the previous one instead of forcing an uninstall that would delete the
# missions saved on the device.
#
# It is committed on purpose and it is PUBLIC. That is acceptable only because
# this app is sideloaded by hand for personal use. It must NEVER be used to sign
# a Play Store release: anyone can read this key out of the repository and sign
# an APK that Android would accept as an update to a store-published app.
# A real release needs a fresh key kept out of version control.
!dev-keystore.jks
!dev-key.properties
